>I'm breezing along through the dungeons of doom (3.1.1) with good armor,
>weapons, intrinsics, etc. I reach the home of Ms. Medusa, and put on my handy
>ring of levitation to float over across the H2O. Anyways, I het attacked by a
>couple of electric eels. No prob, right? (I had shock resistance) Well, they
>all came over and zapped my stuff, destroying all my wands and rings, including
>my ring of levitation. I drowned. Grrrrr...

I have drowned twice, once on the Medusa level and once on the castle
level, due to these lousy eels pulling me into the water.  There is
scarcely any warning.  It says "the eel wraps itself around your leg"
and then the next turn I am dead.  Levitation doesn't help.  The last
time I was even alert for this peril and carefully levitated over to
where my ESP informed me there was only one eel.  "I'll quickly kill
this one while he is alone so they can't gang up on me." I thought.  In
another game I sashayed all the way around the castle moat with a ring
of levitation and had no trouble finishing off the eels.

Presumably an amulet of magical breathing would take care of this
problem?  Next time I will finish the stinking eels off from a distance
or maybe genocide them.



